1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,839
Lumen's Zero-Touch Broker.

2
00:00:02,789 --> 00:00:06,434
Converting network delay into recurring revenue.

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:15,589
Lumen's on-net buildings already connect to Internet On-Demand, Cloud Connect, and software-defined networking.

4
00:00:15,542 --> 00:00:19,850
Eligible, pre-wired capacity can activate without new construction.

5
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:27,509
Buying that capacity still means discovery, solution design, quoting, order entry, and provisioning.

6
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:29,850
A relay race of human hand-offs.

7
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:35,562
Manual hand-offs, API friction, and re-keying lose prospects.

8
00:00:35,512 --> 00:00:39,457
Weeks of quoting leave ready infrastructure unbilled.

9
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:45,451
Our objective: natural language in; a provisioned, billable network out.

10
00:00:45,404 --> 00:00:48,978
Existing customers move from chat to approval.

11
00:00:48,978 --> 00:00:52,850
New prospects move from an office description to a priced plan.

12
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:58,756
Rules check inventory, compare clouds, and calculate exact prices.

13
00:00:58,706 --> 00:01:01,850
AI interprets intent, never pricing.

14
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:06,205
Then, explicit approval unlocks a validated order.

15
00:01:06,156 --> 00:01:09,850
The system checks it against the quote before the provisioning call.

16
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:16,850
The official Lumen Developer Portal defines Multi-Cloud Gateway, Ordering, Quote, and Service Details.

17
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:23,850
The order-request endpoint requires this customer-number header: Lumen's business organization identifier.

18
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:30,698
External ID, billing account, channel, and quote form an explicit request contract.

19
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:36,661
Our local mocks cover ordering, serviceability, quoting, and accounts.

20
00:01:36,611 --> 00:01:39,850
No production circuits or real billing are touched.

21
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:45,006
Five gigabits, with cloud connectivity and DDoS protection.

22
00:01:44,956 --> 00:01:49,188
One clarification: Dallas, and Google Cloud.

23
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:57,750
The quote: six dollars fifteen per hour, four thousand four hundred ninety-three monthly, and zero CapEx.

24
00:01:57,701 --> 00:02:00,850
Six idle ten-gig ports are ready in Dallas.

25
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:05,308
Port, interconnect, egress, and protection.

26
00:02:05,258 --> 00:02:06,850
All itemized.

27
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:09,533
Three clouds compared.

28
00:02:09,483 --> 00:02:11,850
Google Cloud is selected.

29
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:16,850
Follow Dallas, DDoS protection, Lumen's fabric, then Google Cloud.

30
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:20,826
Nothing executes until the customer approves.

31
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:24,807
Site, speed, and price stay aligned.

32
00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:27,164
Mock success.

33
00:02:27,117 --> 00:02:29,850
The demo starts hourly billing immediately.

34
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:38,850
A new prospect describes Apple's Chicago office: five floors, one hundred square feet each, AWS, and DDoS protection.

35
00:02:39,250 --> 00:02:45,264
One click fills company, city, floors, area, cloud, and protection.

36
00:02:45,214 --> 00:02:47,850
All fields remain editable.

37
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:50,586
Chicago is on-net.

38
00:02:50,536 --> 00:02:55,080
Four users, thirty-two megabits, five floor switches.

39
00:02:56,250 --> 00:03:02,138
AWS wins: a dollar eight hourly, saving twenty-four sixty monthly.

40
00:03:02,088 --> 00:03:03,850
Zero CapEx.

41
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:08,850
The full quote and Chicago-to-AWS topology, upfront.

42
00:03:09,250 --> 00:03:13,521
One click creates an account and provisions through our mocks.

43
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:24,267
At the Dallas demo rate, one to three idle weeks represent roughly one to three thousand dollars in delayed gross billings, per connection.

44
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:34,850
Automation lowers acquisition effort, increases network utilization, reduces re-keying fallout, and captures more leads before they leave.

45
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:39,335
Next: live Lumen APIs and contract pricing.

46
00:03:39,285 --> 00:03:42,850
Then enterprise sign-on and account-linked ordering.

47
00:03:43,250 --> 00:03:49,837
Then autonomous scaling, diagnostics, ticketing, and security, with production assurance.

48
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:52,518
Natural language in.

49
00:03:52,468 --> 00:03:55,658
A provisioned, billable network out.

50
00:03:55,659 --> 00:03:57,885
Team ConnectIQ.

51
00:03:57,885 --> 00:03:59,487
Thank you.
